╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ add_individual_parametrized_rotations                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ The current design achieves excellent performance (test accuracy 0.90, generalization gap │
│                          │ 0.01) through heavy parameter sharing with only 4 unique parameters per ansatz block.     │
│                          │ While highly efficient, this aggressive symmetry may limit the model's expressiveness.    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ To improve further, I propose adding individual per-qubit RX rotations after the CZ       │
│                          │ entangler layer. This breaks the collective symmetry in a controlled way, allowing the    │
│                          │ optimizer to learn qubit-specific corrections while maintaining the efficient collective  │
│                          │ structure for the main mixing layers.                                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The new structure will be:                                                                │
│                          │ 1. Collective RY input mixer (shared across all 8 qubits)                                 │
│                          │ 2. Collective RZ phase (shared across all 8 qubits)                                       │
│                          │ 3. CZ entangler (fixed structure)                                                         │
│                          │ 4. **Individual RX rotations on each qubit** (NEW - 8 per block)                          │
│                          │ 5. Collective RY output mixer (shared across all 8 qubits)                                │
│                          │ 6. Collective RX output mixer (shared across all 8 qubits)                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This increases parameters from 26 to ~74 total (12 unique per block × 6 blocks + 2        │
│                          │ readout), a conservative increase that should improve expressiveness while maintaining    │
│                          │ reasonable parameter efficiency and low generalization gap.                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The motivation: individual rotations after entanglement can capture qubit-specific phase  │
│                          │ corrections without breaking the efficient symmetry-preserving design of the main layers. │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0350                                                                                   │
│ error_attempt            │ None                                                                                      │
│ system_prompt_id         │ None                                                                                      │
