│ patch_description        │ The previous candidate achieved a high accuracy (0.90) with very few parameters (26) by   │
│                          │ using total parameter sharing across all qubits in each layer. To further improve         │
│                          │ accuracy while maintaining high parameter efficiency, I propose breaking the global       │
│                          │ symmetry slightly by using parity-based parameter sharing (even vs. odd wires).           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This modification:                                                                        │
│                          │ 1. Increases the number of parameters per block from 4 to 8, allowing for more nuanced    │
│                          │ feature processing without a significant complexity penalty.                              │
│                          │ 2. Replaces the fixed CZ cube with a combination of a CZ hypercube matching and a CNOT    │
│                          │ ring, enhancing the entangling power of each block.                                       │
│                          │ 3. Maintains the sequence of RY, RZ, and RX gates, which are effective for non-commuting  │
│                          │ rotations in the Bloch sphere.                                                            │
│                          │ 4. Total parameters will increase from 26 to 50 (8 params/block * 6 blocks + 2 readout    │
│                          │ params), which remains highly efficient for an 8-qubit system.                            │
