│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ parity_brickwork_mixer                                                                    │
│ patch_description        │ This edit replaces the fully collective 8-qubit layers with a parity-split brickwork      │
│                          │ ansatz.                                                                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Why this should help:                                                                     │
│                          │ - It keeps the same parameter budget per block as the current program (4 trainable angles │
│                          │ per block, 24 total circuit parameters), so efficiency is not sacrificed.                 │
│                          │ - It breaks the overly rigid global symmetry of the seed by giving even and odd qubits    │
│                          │ separate mixers, which is often better for binary-feature data with heterogeneous         │
│                          │ feature-pair couplings.                                                                   │
│                          │ - It reduces gate count substantially by removing the redundant RZ layer and compressing  │
│                          │ the entangling pattern to two staggered CZ matchings.                                     │
│                          │ - The sequence RY -> CZ -> RX -> CZ provides a strong noncommuting mixer-entangler-mixer  │
│                          │ structure that should convert the fixed phase encodings into measurable Z-population      │
│                          │ differences more effectively, while remaining shallow enough to train well.               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Overall, this is a targeted shift toward a lighter, more expressive hardware-efficient    │
│                          │ ansatz that should improve validation/test accuracy and convergence speed while also      │
│                          │ lowering depth and gate count.                                                            │
